<Defs>

  <!--
    ========================================================================
    Jawa_PetNames.xml            Jawa_Patches - authored 2026-08-23
    ========================================================================
    STAR_WARS_PET_NAMES_1. Owner, verbatim: "generate lore-accurate and
    humorous Star Wars pet names as a generator when pets are created or
    tamed. That's important immersion."

    THE RATIO IS 2 LORE : 1 HUMOUR, and it is expressed as grammar WEIGHTS
    rather than in code, so it can be retuned here and nowhere else.
    Rule selection is weighted by p=, so 6:3 is about 67% lore / 33% humour.
    Why two-thirds: the lore register is the TEXTURE and has to be what you
    mostly see, or the setting stops feeling like Star Wars and starts
    feeling like a joke mod. The humour register is CHARACTERISATION - a
    Jawa outfit that names one animal in three "Warranty Void" reads as
    scrappers with a sense of trade; one in two reads as memes.

    72 lore + 60 humour = 132 names. That size is a FLOOR, not a target:
    NameGenerator.GenerateName rejects names already UsedThisGame and retries
    150 times before logging "Could not get new name", so a real menagerie can
    exhaust a small corpus. Appending is one <li>.

    Every output goes through GenText.ToTitleCaseSmart, which capitalises
    after every space and hyphen and lowercases NOTHING - so these are
    written already-cased and nothing surprises you. "M'aloo" survives.

    <li> IS CORRECT HERE. RulePack is a plain class with ordinary List<T>
    fields and no LoadDataFromXmlCustom - this is not the BiomeDef trap
    where an <li> discards the whole def.
    ========================================================================
  -->

